---
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Corner radii" code={'--radius-sm   /* 0.625rem squircle | 0.5rem round: inputs, badges */\n--radius      /* 1.125rem | 0.875rem: buttons, small panels */\n--radius-lg   /* 1.625rem | 1.25rem: tables, panels */\n--radius-xl   /* 2.25rem | 1.75rem: cards and tiles */\n--radius-pill /* 9999px: chips, pills */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Stride's scale. Every rounded surface pairs its radius with <code>corner-shape: var(--corner-shape)</code>.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="radii">
        <div class="radius r-sm"><code>sm</code></div>
        <div class="radius r-md"><code>default</code></div>
        <div class="radius r-lg"><code>lg</code></div>
        <div class="radius r-xl"><code>xl</code></div>
        <div class="radius r-pill"><code>pill</code></div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Squircles" code={'@supports (corner-shape: squircle) { :root { --corner-shape: squircle; /* wider radii */ } }\n@supports not (corner-shape: squircle) { :root { --corner-shape: round; /* narrower radii */ } }'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
        <p>Where the browser supports <code>corner-shape</code>, corners are squircles: continuous superellipse curves instead of circular arcs. Stride branches the whole radius scale on that one feature query: a squircle hugs tighter than a circular corner, so the scale is wider with squircles and narrower without, and the perceived roundness is the same either way.</p>
        <p>Capsules and circles (pills, chips, round icon buttons) keep circular ends; add <code>.round</code> to opt anything else out.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="squircle-compare">
        <figure><div class="sq-sample sq-round"></div><figcaption><code>corner-shape: round</code></figcaption></figure>
        <figure><div class="sq-sample"></div><figcaption><code>corner-shape: squircle</code> (where supported)</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Edges and elevation" surface="alt" code={'border-top: 1px solid var(--edge-light);\nborder-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge-dark);\nbox-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);   /* or --shadow-md, --shadow-lg */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Stride's signature: raised surfaces carry a lit top edge and a shaded bottom edge instead of a border on four sides, so they read as matte panels lifted off the page. In dark mode the light edge is a translucent white overlay, so it works on any surface. Shadows stay soft.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="tile elev"><code>edges + --shadow-sm</code></div>
        <div class="tile elev elev-md"><code>edges + --shadow-md</code></div>
        <div class="tile elev elev-lg"><code>edges + --shadow-lg</code></div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Recessed surfaces" code={'<div class="surface surface-recessed">…</div>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The inverse: a panel below the page, with the dark edge on top and the light edge beneath. Used for card footers and secondary panels.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="surface border-sample"><code>.surface</code></div>
        <div class="surface surface-recessed border-sample"><code>.surface-recessed</code></div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<style>
    .radii {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .radius {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        width: 7rem;
        height: 7rem;
        background: var(--bg-alt);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }

    .radius { corner-shape: var(--corner-shape); }
    .r-sm { border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
    .r-md { border-radius: var(--radius); }
    .r-lg { border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
    .r-xl { border-radius: var(--radius-xl); }
    .r-pill { width: 10rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: var(--radius-pill); corner-shape: round; }

    .squircle-compare {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 2rem;
    }

    .squircle-compare figure {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        justify-items: center;
    }

    .squircle-compare figcaption {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }

    .sq-sample {
        width: 10rem;
        height: 10rem;
        border-radius: 2.5rem;
        corner-shape: squircle;
        background: var(--brand-gradient);
    }

    .sq-round {
        corner-shape: round;
    }

    .elev {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        height: 9rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }

    .elev-md { box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); }
    .elev-lg { box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg); }

    .border-sample {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        height: 6rem;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }


</style>
